{
  "_readme": [
    "Beat-reporter source registry. This is DATA, not code -- a dead feed is a",
    "one-line edit here, no Python change and no redeploy logic to touch.",
    "",
    "Source types:",
    "  rss     -- a direct RSS/Atom feed URL. Highest reliability.",
    "  gnews   -- a Google News RSS search, built from `query`. Used for named",
    "             beat writers whose outlet has no clean per-author feed.",
    "  bluesky -- public.api.bsky.app getAuthorFeed for `actor` (a handle or DID).",
    "",
    "The Beat Feed page shows a source-health panel listing every source that",
    "failed, so anything stale here is visible rather than silently missing.",
    "Team keys are Sleeper's NFL team abbreviations.",
    "",
    "X beat writers are batched by DIVISION: 8 calls cover all 32 teams instead of 32. Team attribution survives batching via the x_handles map, so the By Team tab still works. Fewer, larger batches mean fewer pulls but a shared 20-tweet budget per call -- fine on a 10-minute refresh, thinner after a long gap."
  ],
